From 361c489295cdb90602a06bb960ba3d582340eef5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Janice <djanice1980@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 08:41:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: log FRL loss of lock and recovery at warning
 level (local)

The retrain request added by the previous patch printed through FRL_INFO, i.e.
drm_dbg, so it is invisible unless drm.debug=0x2 is set by hand. That makes the
event unprovable in normal use: the display either recovers or it does not, and
the journal says nothing either way.

Promote the loss-of-lock request to DC_LOG_WARNING and add a matching line when
the sink reports lock again, so an ordinary journal records the pair:

  HDMI FRL: sink reports loss of lock (status=0x40) with rate=5 active -- requesting retrain
  HDMI FRL: sink lock restored (status=0x5f)

One line per 5 s at most while unlocked, nothing at all on a healthy link.
---
 .../gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_hdmi_frl.c  | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_hdmi_frl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_hdmi_frl.c
index 928fd68..b022d16 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_hdmi_frl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_hdmi_frl.c
@@ -293,12 +293,15 @@ bool hdmi_frl_poll_status_flag(struct dc_link *link)
 				dm_get_elapse_time_in_ns(link->ctx, now, frl_last_retrain_ts)
 					> 5000000000ULL) {
 			frl_last_retrain_ts = now;
-			FRL_INFO("FRL WATCHDOG: sink reports link down (status=0x%02x) with rate=%d active"
-					" -- requesting retrain\n",
+			DC_LOG_WARNING("HDMI FRL: sink reports loss of lock (status=0x%02x)"
+					" with rate=%d active -- requesting retrain\n",
 					scdc_status.byte, link->frl_link_settings.frl_link_rate);
 			link_update = true;
 		}
 	} else if (scdc_status.fields.CH0_LOCKED) {
+		if (frl_last_retrain_ts != 0)
+			DC_LOG_WARNING("HDMI FRL: sink lock restored (status=0x%02x)\n",
+					scdc_status.byte);
 		frl_last_retrain_ts = 0;
 	}
 
